  (text "amplitude" (at 41.91 64.1 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify right bottom)) (uuid 14aff28f-317d-40ff-a847-d970b12550de))
  (text "wick" (at 41.91 97.12 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify right bottom)) (uuid a7b4ef09-e788-4362-b832-42606febd38e))
  (text "fall" (at 41.91 130.14 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify right bottom)) (uuid 878f3ae8-1aa3-4483-bda2-cee3adb6be4a))
  (text "knee, power axis" (at 41.91 163.16 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify right bottom)) (uuid 68ae5f64-a27f-4bfe-85a1-a847d3488d51))
  (text "pulse width" (at 41.91 196.18 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify right bottom)) (uuid cd73014a-4fc3-4734-a514-7f81ec5c4e3b))
  (text "pulse rate" (at 41.91 229.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify right bottom)) (uuid ef582080-ea1f-4d0f-9454-a4920dc44114))
  (text "knee, time axis" (at 41.91 262.22 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify right bottom)) (uuid f5fd779a-c93e-454d-90aa-71d2febfbacb))
  (text "KNOBS are off-board, NO extra resistors: each wiper goes straight to its ESP32 pin through J1.2…J1.8 (one wire each).\nThe 3V3 (J1.1) and GND (J1.9) rails are daisy-chained from pot to pot — one pair of wires from the board, 3.3 V across every pot." (at 101.6 294.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 34bd7184-cdb5-43af-b557-d77fd0c95001))
  (text "BUTTONS are off-board: FIRE and AUTO on J2/J3 (signal, GND), pull-ups inside the ESP32.\nE-STOP is one switch with two contact groups, two 2-wire cables: J4 (group A, NO) shorts GPIO23 to ground; J8 (group B, NC) is in series with the U1 input." (at 38.1 388.62 0) (effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 7bc9b514-e79b-4af9-a1d7-d0899371b3a1))
  (text "AUTO (TX2=GPIO17), FIRE (RX2=GPIO16): labels go to J3/J2." (at 320.04 208.28 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 6f4ddb15-0481-4812-9c10-d10c01507d88))
  (text "E-STOP group A: GPIO23 -> label ESTOP_A -> J4.1; the switch shorts it to J4.2 = GND. 4.7k to 3V3 and 100n at the pin." (at 306.07 63.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 28a2f2bf-3e04-47ef-8785-e8a5ac0f1751))
  (text "DISPLAY is off-board, 5-wire cable to J5:\n1 GND -> CN1.GND, 2 SCL -> CN1.IO22, 3 SDA -> CN1.IO27,\n4 VMETER -> P3.IO35, 5 +5V -> display USB/VIN.\n4.7k pull-ups and the 10k/10k divider are on the board.\nCN1.3V3 is not used." (at 459.74 106.68 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 9ff54a9b-52a0-491c-8f24-66f04d455cea))
  (text "VOLTMETER: R18 from +5V to node VMETER, R19 from the node to GND;\nthe display shows e.g. 5.0V in small font: green >4.8 V, yellow, red <4.5 V." (at 459.74 121.92 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 1826663a-bd1b-4d35-80ce-d824def7d2d0))
  (text "non-inverting!" (at 356.87 185.39 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 2b0719b0-59f3-440f-b51d-c84e7f978364))
  (text "HFBR-1412/1414 transmitter is off-board, 2-wire cable to J: 1 = anode (pins 2, 6, 7 tied together),\n2 = cathode (pin 3). Pins 1/4/5/8 unused. It needs no supply: ~60 mA comes from the TC4420 through 2x100 ohm." (at 454.66 208.28 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid bd7bf377-36cf-4bce-b070-bf5e1cbd1a95))
  (text "BUCK CHANNEL (ramp): GPIO19 -> 150 -> U2 -> 2x100 -> J6" (at 317.5 144.78 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 5547cd71-994c-44f8-b0a1-fdd8dfbf5ec2))
  (text "non-inverting!" (at 361.95 259.05 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid fdf324f9-4435-4eb1-b60c-3dff690ffa93))
  (text "HFBR-1412/1414 transmitter is off-board, 2-wire cable to J: 1 = anode (pins 2, 6, 7 tied together),\n2 = cathode (pin 3). Pins 1/4/5/8 unused. It needs no supply: ~60 mA comes from the TC4420 through 2x100 ohm." (at 454.66 281.94 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 47b82217-0346-4b39-a0f7-a72a99387017))
  (text "BRIDGE CHANNEL (interrupter): GPIO4 -> 150 -> E-STOP group B (J8, NC) -> U1 -> 2x100 -> J7 -> D1" (at 317.5 219.71 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid bc026cd3-6c52-494d-80a2-b3e62bf2f191))
  (text "Light = bridge enabled; broken fiber = dark = inhibit. On the driver board set J1 to position C-B (light = ON)." (at 317.5 294.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 63082608-2879-4dc6-a841-66121acd1f40))
  (text "optical fiber" (at 480.06 170.18 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 2730262d-546b-4e88-83b2-4698dbfb9048))
  (text "optical fiber" (at 490.22 242.57 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 1bc39cad-3ffc-45b1-97d2-8dd81996e3de))
  (text "DRIVER BOARD (qcw_driver)\nRX buck    HFBR-2412 <- fiber from D2\nRX bridge  HFBR-2412 <- fiber from D1\nReceiver: dark = HIGH.\nJumper J1: position C-B\n(light = ON, broken fiber = OFF).\nReceivers: 2 = Vcc +5 V of that board,\n3 and 7 = common, 6 = output.\nNO galvanic connection to the controller." (at 510.54 250.19 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 35cfa271-6e88-47cb-b805-1b6866d40f32))
  (text "POWER: battery -> off-board buck converter -> screw terminal J9 (1 = +5 V, 2 = GND). On the board +5 V feeds ESP32 VIN, U1/U2 VDD, R18 and J5.5 (display).\n3V3 comes from the ESP32 module (to J1…J7 and the pull-ups). Ground: buck minus = J9.2; the whole board ground is the bottom-layer pour. Enclosure to J9.2 with a single wire.\nOff-board (on_board=no): RV1…RV7, SW1…SW4, A2 display, D1/D2 transmitters, PS1, BT1. Labels with the same name = one net (cable <-> board)." (at 190.5 340.36 0) (effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 6b0fba67-c264-40c1-b409-f20970ae9d32))
  (text "QCW DRSSTC CONTROLLER v5.9-ESP32 — schematic for the control board (rev. E, 2026-09-27): ESP32 DevKit in socket headers, 2x TC4420 DIP-8, through-hole resistors, SMD 1206 capacitors (on the copper side), knobs daisy-chained on J1, everything else on J2…J9." (at 38.1 17.78 0) (effects (font (size 1.7 1.7)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid f050d581-83fb-457d-ba46-fae724ac0530))
